.jaato

# ...except an eval task's config root, which is DATA, not a developer's
# local settings: it is the read-only half of the task definition
# (profiles, agents, permissions) and must travel with the repository.
# The directory itself has to be un-ignored before the negation on its
# contents can apply — git does not descend into an excluded directory.
!jaato-eval/tasks/*/.jaato/
!jaato-eval/tasks/*/.jaato/**

# Eval scratch workspaces.  ``jaato_eval run --workspaces`` materialises one
# fixture copy (and one git worktree) per arm here; a sweep leaves hundreds
# of megabytes behind when run with --keep-workspaces.  Ignored under any
# parent so a misresolved workspace root — the #742 failure, which dropped
# 341 MB of worktrees into the framework repo — is never one ``git add -A``
# from being committed.
.jaato-eval-workspaces/
